This puts me in mind of a trick I use to rob shops.  Usually, when I walk
into a shop my dog runs ahead of me and eats all the tripe rations, which
makes training him very difficult.  I have gotten in the habit of carrying
a cursed item around with me to avoid this problem.  When I find a shop if
I have a cursed item, I drop it in the doorway and search the store to
see if I can find a tripe ration _before_ my doggy comes in and eats them
all.  If I don't have a cursed item, I close the door and go and find one.
This generally works pretty well.  Regarding the problem laid out earlier,
getting your dog to drop stuff next to you in this situation

-----------+#
.........@.P#  @ = Asidonhopo
.......d..X|   P = You
...........|   d = dog
...........|   X = spot your dog drops damned items no matter how much
-----------+       you feed the mutt.

Just take a step back...The dog will now bring items and drop them in
the doorway.


